From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anaconda Recipes <recipe-maintainers@anaconda.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Use protobuf's proto_library/cc_proto_library in kernels BUILD

The OSS export relies on Bazel's builtin proto rules, whose cc_proto_aspect
requires the toolchain target to provide the builtin ProtoLangToolchainInfo.
@com_google_protobuf//:cc_toolchain comes from protobuf-bazel-rules and
provides protobuf's own provider, so analysis failed with
"rule 'proto_lang_toolchain' does not contain declared provider
'ProtoLangToolchainInfo'".

Load protobuf's rules, as upstream does internally, so both sides use the
same provider.
---
 tensorflow_text/core/kernels/BUILD | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tensorflow_text/core/kernels/BUILD b/tensorflow_text/core/kernels/BUILD
--- a/tensorflow_text/core/kernels/BUILD
+++ b/tensorflow_text/core/kernels/BUILD
@@ -4,9 +4,9 @@ load("@flatbuffers//:build_defs.bzl", "flatbuffer_cc_library")
 load("@rules_cc//cc:cc_library.bzl", "cc_library")
 load("@rules_cc//cc:cc_test.bzl", "cc_test")
 
-# Placeholder: load proto_library
+load("@com_google_protobuf//bazel:proto_library.bzl", "proto_library")
 load("//tensorflow_text:tftext.bzl", "tf_cc_library", "tflite_cc_library")
-# [internal] load cc_proto_library.bzl
+load("@com_google_protobuf//bazel:cc_proto_library.bzl", "cc_proto_library")
 
 licenses(["notice"])
 
